    "https://www.nmt.edu/hr/Postdoctoral%20Research%20Scientist-job%20advertisement.pdf": {
      "title": "POSTDOCTORAL RESEARCH SCIENTIST/ POWER AND ENERGY SYSTEMS",
      "description": " \n \nPOSTDOCTORAL RESEARCH SCIENTIST/ POWER AND ENERGY SYSTEMS \nPosition Type: Full Time \nSalary Range: $55,000 - $60,000 \nNew Mexico Tech (NMT) invites applications for a postdoctoral research fellow position in the \nbroad area of power and energy systems. This is a joint position between the Petroleum Recovery \nResearch Center (PRRC) and the Department of Electrical Engineerin g. The initial appointment \nwill be for 12 months and can be extended based on performance. The position presents an \nexcellent career development opportunity with an interdisciplinary team at NMT. The postdoctoral \nresearch fellow is expected to participate in project research activities while interacting with \ngraduate and undergraduate research assistants. There will be peer-reviewed publications, proposal \ndevelopment, and other training opportunities. \n \nRequired Qualifications: \n• Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Power Systems, Power Electronics, Energy Systems, or \nother related fields;  \n• Strong research background in power and energy systems, preferably in smart grids, \nmicrogrids, or distributed energy resources;  \n• Familiar with MATLAB, Python, and other programming tools; \n• Excellent writing and oral communication skills. \n \nPreferred Qualifications: \n• Hands-on experience with power system hardware, real -time simulation (OPAL -RT, \nRTDS, Typhoon HIL, etc), hardware-in-the-loop (HIL/PHIL), or laboratory experiments;  \n• Experience with microgrid or smart grid testbeds; \n• Experience integrating distributed energy resources, power electronics, or control systems; \n• Familiarity with communication protocols (IEC 61850, Modbus, DNP3, etc); \n• Experience in grant proposal writing. \n \nPosition open until filled; for status of the position, please send inquiries to Dr. Qingsong Cui at \nqingsong.cui@nmt.edu. To apply, please email your application package in a single PDF \ndocument to nmtjobapps@npe.nmt.edu and copy to qingsong.cui@nmt.edu and \nsai.wang@nmt.edu, with \" NMT-Postdoc-PES\" in the email subject line. The package should \ncontain a cover letter highlighting expertise and experience most suited to the position, the most \nrecent CV, transcript(s), representative publications, and contact information of 2–3 references. \nNMT is committed to creating a community in which a diverse population can learn, live, and \nwork in an atmosphere of tolerance, civility and respect for the rights and sensibilities of each \nindividual. NMT is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NMT provides exc ellent benefits, including \nhealth, vision, dental, and a generous retirement plan. \n  \n"
    }
